WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-A few corrections --

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to do a few corrections
from yesterday.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yesterday, I was talking about
the children's character -

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:09.776
the children's book character --
excuse me -- Babar,

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.577 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Babar the Elephant.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said "Buh-bar,"
and I was told that was wrong.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.116 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's "Bah-bar."

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.384 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I was saying it like

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:20.387
David Spade's "Flight Attendant"
character.

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:21.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Buh-bar."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were talking about it
because --

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
because
of the context of Dr. Seus

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how Babar is just
getting away with the fact

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he married
his cousin Celeste.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But that's helpful

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:41.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause he answers to Babar
King of the Elephants,

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.077 line:92%
and Giuliani of the Jungle..

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.081 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
...but not Buh-bar.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:48.782 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Also, I said we --

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:55.088
we referred to "cliffhanger"
in German as "Klippenbuegel.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was told
by some German viewers

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the German word
for "cliffhanger"

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
is "Cliffhanger."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:06.366
So German is a little bit easier
to learn than I thought.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.367 line:92%
And that Klippenbuegel --

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.935 size:81% position:41%
obviously, we're upset
that we got it wrong.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:15.141
We are gonna take it up with our
on-staff German fact-checker

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.077 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Klaus Google-Translate.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.647 line:92%
I was told the way we said i

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
was basically like
a coat hanger on a cliff,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.752 line:92%
and as a means of apology,

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
here's what
that would look like.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.692 line:92%
The real bad one, though, is

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said the word
"surreptitiously."

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:40.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
I pronounced it
"sir-rip-it-ously"...

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.602 line:92%
which is, of course, the German.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It's pretty bad.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Sir-rip-it-ously"
is not a good --

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
I missed both T's,
which is pretty embarrassing

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I came in today
and I said to Shoemaker,

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:55.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Did you --
Did you notice that I said

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:56.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
'surreptitishly' --
[chuckles]

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you notice I said
'surreptitiously' wrong?"

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said
"No, because I thought

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were saying
a different word."

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"Yeah, but in context,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.192 line:92%
didn't you -- didn't you know?

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.195
He goes, "I actually think
you also used it wrong."

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.563 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.664 line:92%
So that's a real double barrel

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also,
you might have thought tha

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
once I said it
"sir-rip-it-ously,"

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.769 size:78% position:39%
I internally thought,
"That's not right."

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.705 line:92%
Absolutely, 100% not the case.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said it and thought,
"Nailed it."

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.511 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:27.213 line:92%
Walked home proud of myself.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.715 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.316
But, again -- and
I also want to point out that --

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, when I make mistakes
and you guys call them out

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.487
and then I take time on the show
to correct them,

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
that doesn't mean you should
keep pointing them out.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:41.261 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if you want to,
that's fine.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.364 line:92%
That's your pre-go-itive.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.199 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.301 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But...

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.002 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.237 size:75% position:38%
...we're just trying
to do our best here.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.705 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

